# uv.lock IS committed on purpose (exact-version authority, ADR-10)
# (anchored to repo root so they never swallow docs/journal/)

# --- Claude Code control plane: NOT part of this repository ---
# The harness (agents, skills, hooks, rules, commands, settings) is tooling,
# not Sanad. It was taken out of the repo across PRs #25, #28 and #29, came
# back at project level in PR #31, and is now out again for good.
#
# Two reasons it does not belong here. It buried Sanad's own ~770-node code
# graph under thousands of nodes of vendored payload and failed ruff on lines
# that were never Sanad's; and a reviewer grading a story diff should never
# have to page through harness churn to find the twenty lines that are the
# actual change.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly rather than discovered later: any local repair
# to .claude/hooks/ now lives on ONE machine and is invisible to the other
# teammate. Durable hook fixes belong in ~/.claude/hooks/, which is what every
# project on a machine reads from.
.claude/

# MCP server wiring is machine-local for the same reason .claude/ is. On this
# machine it has to name an absolute path to the 0.10.8 binary, because the
# `codebase-memory-mcp` shim on PATH is a stale npm 0.10.5 and loses a version
# race to the already-running server, so the tools never attach. That path
# carries a username and a Windows-only layout; committing it hands the other
# teammate a config that fails silently rather than loudly. The durable fix is
# to update the global install so PATH resolves to the current binary, after
# which no absolute path is needed here at all.
.mcp.json

# --- Agent worktrees (live git worktrees; never a tracked gitlink) ---
.claude/worktrees/

# --- Per-agent scratch memory (machine-local, unreviewed, goes stale) ---
# Durable facts belong in docs/journal/BUILD-STATE.md and DECISIONS.md, which
# are reviewed and versioned. Committing agent memory would duplicate those
# and let an unreviewed copy contradict them.
.claude/agent-memory/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Local backups and archives (never tracked) ---
*.bak
*.zip
*.bak
*.retired
.claude.json
**/node_modules/
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.key
*.pem
settings.local.json
evals/fixture/node_modules/

# --- Local code-graph artifact (regenerated, not shared) ---
.codebase-memory/

# --- Stray duplicates from botched extracts ---
# Windows drops these when an archive is unpacked over existing files.
# 'README copy.md' is the harness's own README, not Sanad's.
* copy
* copy.*
